## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

B295 takeover leaves unremovable ghost room members. Neither backends takeover path touches room membership (only the 12-month release_alias does: relay.ml:728-731, 2561-2564). After a rename takeover the old alias keeps its room_members rows but has no lease: identity_pk_of returns None and verify_room_op_proof (relay.ml:5888-5899) rejects its leave_room, no peer can kick it (uninvite only edits the invite ACL), and only /admin/unbind clears it. Every subsequent send_room to that room skips the ghost (sqlite) or additionally appends a full-content recipient_dead dead-letter row per message (in-memory, relay.ml:1505-1517) - an unbounded, content-bearing log fed by other members traffic.

## Fix direction

On pair takeover, remove the shadowed aliases from room_members in both backends, matching release_alias semantics.

## Evidence

Server-core review 2026-09-17.